We thank reviewers for their thoughtful feedback. We are encouraged that they find our submission provides reusable insight (MpYY), our motivations is clear (MpYY), the F-LN problem is important and realistic (29PX, 1rw9, MpYY), and our presentation is good (29PX, 1rw9). We are also glad they find our extensive evaluation results under board F-LNL setups are sound (29PX, 1rw9, MpYY).

We have updated the revision following all reviewers' suggestions (text in blue). We hope our responses can address all the reviewers’ concerns. FYI, the main changes are listed below:

- **Update experimental results**: 

  - In the main paper, we have:
    - added a hyperparameter analysis of $\gamma_g$ and $\gamma_l$ (Table 7);
    - added ablation results on the warm‑up strategy, removing the assumption that all clients are sampled during warm‑up (Table 5);
    - improved the illustration of the Pearson correlation analysis and clients’ F‑score distributions (Fig. 4).

  - In the appendix, we have:

    - added results on CIFAR‑10/100 and Clothing1M reported with best accuracy (Tables 10–11);
    - added additional empirical observations under different noise ratios and client scales (Fig. 12);
    - added the test‑accuracy curve on Clothing1M (Fig. 5);
    - added visualizations of the GMM fitting results (Fig. 23).

- **Revise experimental analysis**: We updated and refined the experimental analysis to incorporate and discuss the new results in more detail.
- **Fix presentation issues**: We corrected several presentation issues noted by the reviewers, improved the consistency of mathematical notation, and added a notation table in the appendix to facilitate understanding. We also revise the motivation in Sec. 3.4 and append an algorithmic illustration (Fig. 3) to make this part clearer and more accessible.

If the SACs, ACs, and reviewers have any further questions and concerns, we are very glad to respond and discuss them.
